Recover scheduled goal wakes

App-server restart and session unload can discard process-local
supervisor ownership while an active goal and wake schedule remain
durable.

Let the app server discover bounded active-root candidates, revalidate
their persisted wake identity, and cold-resume due goals under a
per-home ownership lock. Unload scheduler-materialized roots only after
the goal is inactive and the supervisor runtime is quiescent.

Cover recovery with an external client clock and no subscribed client
so the app server remains responsible for unattended wake execution.
